  "problem": "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}+5{y}^{″}-3{t}^{2}{y}^{′}=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & a & c\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$",
